<title>FINLAND: HELSINKI-VANTAA AIRPORT STRIKES CALLED OFF - TV.</title>
<headline>HELSINKI-VANTAA AIRPORT STRIKES CALLED OFF - TV.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The transport workers union's strike among airport bus drivers which started on Monday at 0600/0400 GMT was called off at about 0830/0630 GMT, Finnish television news reported.</p>
<p>The planned support strike by airport fuel truckers which would have made at least domestic air traffic difficult was also called off, it said.</p>
<p>The airport bus drivers wanted a collective agreement and now got one since the employers -- airport services company Suomen Lentoasemapalvelut Oy, owned by the Finnish aviation authority -- did not want to take resposibility for the planned support strike, TV news said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 245</p>
